                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "86a8ba2b-6fec-316a-be51-bf583fb79ca5",
                        "entry_id": "24368114-11a1-3364-80d6-c6421a0ddbda",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Resembling a slap, especially of sound."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "938750f0-3c04-4f30-b68c-3e6aa7a03d77",
                                "sense_id": "86a8ba2b-6fec-316a-be51-bf583fb79ca5",
                                "text": "Where the laughing-gull scoots by the slappy shore and laughs her near-human laugh"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fba4883e-03b1-4f21-bb8b-579e2f09e305",
                                "sense_id": "86a8ba2b-6fec-316a-be51-bf583fb79ca5",
                                "text": "Katy thought about the damp yellow bodies which often landed, with a slappy sound in a burst of moisture and steam rose off them because they were parted from the warmth of their mothers."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5ac36536-25b9-4fd3-b62b-225ac900ee77",
                                "sense_id": "86a8ba2b-6fec-316a-be51-bf583fb79ca5",
                                "text": "Thin picks flex too much and make your wrist work overtime, plus they tend to produce a slappy tone. Those heavy picks popular with today's bluegrass mandolinists are really too stiff for playing the rapid triplets in some Irish tunes."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5e635f7b-ac38-480e-8c12-d178fd9142a3",
                                "sense_id": "86a8ba2b-6fec-316a-be51-bf583fb79ca5",
                                "text": "Jill had Mark apply sunscreen to her back.\n\"Bet these river guides get a lot of skin cancer\", he said. He had a slappy, unpleasant way of doing it, and she struggled to keep her balance."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
